```

IMPORTANT: The file may be large. Build it piece by piece using multiple fs_write calls (create first chunk, then append remaining chunks).

IMPORTANT: Both libraries use global mutable state (stbds_hash_seed). Each test that calls stbds_rand_seed or any hash function must be careful. Use stbds_rand_seed to set the same seed in both libraries before each test.

IMPORTANT: stbds_hash_seed is a global static in each .so. When you call stbds_rand_seed on the C lib, it sets C's seed. When you call it on Rust lib, it sets Rust's seed. They are independent. So always set the same seed on both before comparing hash outputs.

IMPORTANT: stbds_arrgrowf returns a pointer offset by sizeof(StbdsArrayHeader) from the allocation. The header is at ptr-1 (in header units). The header struct is:
```c
typedef struct {
  size_t length;
  size_t capacity;
  void *hash_table;
  ptrdiff_t temp;
} stbds_array_header;
```
So sizeof = 32 bytes on 64-bit. When testing arrgrowf, you can check the header fields.

Here are the exported C functions to test (signatures):

```c
void stbds_rand_seed(size_t seed);
